     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":2,\"rationale\":\"Blocking iotDevice:exploitPublicApp and appServer:lateralMovement makes the target unreachable. Blocking iotDevice cuts off memoryDump, which in turn removes printServer, rdpLogin, monitoringHost and vpnSession. That kills mailArchive and dbReplica. It also kills serviceAccount (needs printServer) and secretsManager (needs vpnSession), so shareMount is gone. The only remaining route to vaultRead is appServer, which is still reachable through configSecret from containerHost and supplychain, so appServer must be blocked as well. One block is not enough: the appServer route via configSecret does not pass through iotDevice or memoryDump, and the printServer route does not pass through appServer, so no single step lies on every attack path.\"}"
    }
   ],
